+# Extending
+
+How to add features so the fork stays easy to sync as it grows. The Claude
+Code skill `/fork-change` follows this guide.
+
+## Where new code goes
+
+Prefer the first option that works. Each step down this table costs more on
+every sync.
+
+| You want to add | Put it in | Plugs in through |
+|---|---|---|
+| A brand value (name, URL, User-Agent) | `strix/jitera/brand.py` | `brand.current()` |
+| A default for an upstream setting | `ENV_DEFAULTS` in `strix/jitera/bootstrap.py` | The environment, before upstream starts |
+| A setting users should know | `.env.example` | Read from `.env` on every run |
+| An agent tool | `strix/jitera/tools/<name>.py` (`@function_tool`) | `register_agent_tools` (upstream hook) |
+| Pentest knowledge, or a replacement for an upstream skill | `strix/jitera/skills/<category>/<name>.md` | `register_skill_dir` (upstream hook) |
+| A CLI subcommand | `strix/jitera/commands/<name>.py` | `COMMANDS`, dispatched by the bootstrap |
+| An external service as a tool | An MCP server | `~/.strix/mcp-servers.json`; no code |
+| Behavior upstream has no hook for | A minimal edit to the upstream file | Recorded as a patch |
+| A generic bug fix | A PR to `usestrix/strix` first | Comes back on the next sync |
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    run["jitera-pentest"] --> boot["strix/jitera/bootstrap.py"]
+    boot --> env["load .env;<br/>JITERA_PENTEST_* → STRIX_*;<br/>defaults (telemetry off)"]
+    boot --> brand["activate the Jitera brand"]
+    boot --> hooks["register our tools and skills"]
+    boot --> cmds{"our subcommand?"}
+    cmds -- yes --> ours["strix/jitera/commands/"]
+    cmds -- no --> strix["upstream Strix CLI, unchanged"]
+```
+
+## Rules that keep sync cheap
+
+- **Never rename upstream internals.** The `strix` package, `STRIX_*`
+  settings, `~/.strix`, the Go module path and class names stay as they are.
+- **Keep in-place edits small.** Change the line you need, not the
+  function around it. No reformatting of nearby code.
+- **Read brand values; don't hardcode them.** In an upstream file, put
+  `from strix.jitera import brand  # noqa: E402  (Jitera fork)` on its own line
+  just above the first use, then read `brand.current().name` and so on.
+- **Keep upstream's tests green without editing them.** Upstream tests run with
+  the Strix brand profile; only `jitera-pentest` switches to ours. Our tests go
+  in `tests/jitera/`.
+- **Replace a whole file only when you must**, and list it in `fork/OWNED`.
+- **Rebuild generated files; never patch them.** The viewer bundle
+  (`make viewer`) and `uv.lock` (`uv lock`, with a current uv).
+- **Run uv with `--frozen`.** An outdated uv rewrites `uv.lock`.
+
+## The change loop
+
+1. Edit the code. Run it with `uv run --frozen jitera-pentest …`.
+2. `git add` new files, then `fork/dev test`.
+3. If the change affects what the agent does, run the eval (see
+   [eval-driven development](eval-driven-development.md)).
+4. `fork/dev save`, and write the `Title:` / `Why:` header of any new patch to
+   an upstream file.
+5. Commit the code and its patches together, and open a PR.
+
+## Scaling the team
+
+| Need | Provided by |
+|---|---|
+| One way to do everything | `fork/dev help` |
+| Guided changes in Claude Code | `/fork-change`, `/fork-sync`, `/eval-run`, `/eval-gepa` |
+| Review that sees real code | Code is edited in place; patches are a by-product |
+| A shared definition of done | The eval gate, plus the PR template checklist |
+| Settings without tribal knowledge | `.env.example` |
